# Walter backup restore guide

Backups are made nightly at about 03:30 UTC (plus up to 10 minutes of random delay) by
`spark-backup.timer` running `/usr/local/sbin/spark-backup.sh`. Snapshots go to
`${MODELS_DIR}/backups/<YYYY-mm-dd_HHMM>/`. `${MODELS_DIR}` is a separate XFS disk from the root disk.
Retention keeps the newest snapshot of each of the last 14 days plus the newest of each of the
last 8 Sundays. `${MODELS_DIR}/backups/LAST_OK` names the last successful snapshot. Everything is
root-only (dirs 700, files 600) and is **not encrypted** locally. Snapshots contain all secrets: .env
files, keys and DB dumps.

Logs: `journalctl -u spark-backup`. Run a backup now: `sudo systemctl start spark-backup`.
